# Commercial S4 evidence index self-reference

## Safe code

`S4_EVIDENCE_INDEX_INCLUDED_ITSELF`

## Result

After the failed-readiness run was safely stopped and its window closed, an ad-hoc evidence-index command opened `EVIDENCE-SHA256SUMS` before enumerating files. The enumeration therefore included the index being written and the strict check correctly reported one mismatch.

No service or product state was affected. All underlying evidence files remain private and unchanged.

## Correction

The versioned finalizer builds the index in a root-private temporary file outside the evidence directory, explicitly excludes `EVIDENCE-SHA256SUMS`, atomically installs the completed index, and then performs a strict verification. It is invoked automatically by future `close-window` actions and can re-finalize the closed failed-run evidence read-only with respect to its captured members.
